IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `lta-types`
IMPORT `lta-repair`

-- Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK) — GOAL 3: INFORMATION ABOUT THE
-- LANDLORD (ss 1, 3, 22).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1985-70.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — information about the landlord`

-- s 1(1): the statement of the landlord's name and address must be supplied
-- "within the period of 21 days beginning with the day on which he receives
-- the request" — the last day is receipt + 20.
@ref s 1(1)
@export The last day for a rent collector or agent to supply a tenant with the landlord's name and address under s 1 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK): the end of the 21 days beginning with the day the written request was received (receipt + 20). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN received IS A DATE  @desc The day the written request was received
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to disclose the landlord's identity after a request received on` received MEANS
    `the day` 20 `days after` received

-- s 3(1): the new landlord must give notice "not later than the next day on
-- which rent is payable under the tenancy or, if that is within two months of
-- the assignment, the end of that period of two months". The two months end
-- on the corresponding date two months after the assignment.
@ref s 3(1)
@export The last day for a new landlord to give the tenant written notice of the assignment and of its name and address under s 3(1) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK): the next rent day, or, if that falls within two months of the assignment, the end of those two months. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN assigned IS A DATE   @desc The day of the assignment
      rentDay  IS A DATE   @desc The next day on which rent is payable
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for notice of an assignment on` assigned `with next rent day` rentDay MEANS
    IF   rentDay AT MOST twoMonths
    THEN twoMonths
    ELSE rentDay
    WHERE
        twoMonths MEANS `add months` assigned 2

-- s 3(3A)-(3B): the old landlord stays liable for breaches "occurring before
-- the end of the relevant period", which ends with the date when notice is
-- given by the new landlord, or by the old landlord, "whichever happens
-- first". NOTHING: no notice yet.
@ref s 3(3A)-(3B)
@export The last day of the period in which the old landlord remains liable to the tenant under s 3(3A)-(3B) of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 (UK): the day the first written notice of the assignment (by the new or the old landlord) is given; NOTHING while neither has given notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN f IS A `Landlord information facts`  @desc The days notice of the assignment was given by the new and by the old landlord
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the end of the old landlord's liability under` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `new landlord's notice given on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN f's `old landlord's notice given on`
    WHEN JUST n THEN
        CONSIDER f's `old landlord's notice given on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST n
        WHEN JUST o THEN JUST (IF n AT MOST o THEN n ELSE o)

-- s 22(2): the tenant "may within six months of obtaining the summary require
-- the landlord in writing to afford him reasonable facilities". (4): "for a
-- period of two months beginning not later than one month after the request
-- is made."
@ref s 22(2)
GIVEN obtained IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to request inspection after a summary obtained on` obtained MEANS
    `add months` obtained 6

@ref s 22(4)
GIVEN requested IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest start of the inspection facilities after a request on` requested MEANS
    `add months` requested 1
